**Definition 6.1 (exact common-decoder coincidence set).** Put

$$
q_{\rm abs}=\left(1,
 \frac1{\sqrt{\alpha+\beta t_+^2}},
 \frac{t_+}{\sqrt{\alpha+\beta t_+^2}}\right)^T
\tag{TA.37}
$$

and define a set of original required thresholds

$$
\mathcal E_{\rm abs}=
 \{s_0\tau(a):0<a<a_\dagger,\ k=k(a),\ W(a,k)^Tq_{\rm abs}=0\}.
\tag{TA.38}
$$

Equivalently retain all real solutions of
$\mathcal P(a,k)=0$ and $W(a,k)^Tq_{\rm abs}=0$ in
$0<a<a_\dagger$, $7/20<k<2/5$, and map them by $s=s_0\tau(a)$.
The selected $k$ is essential; arbitrary polynomial roots are excluded.

